<title>GREECE: NATL INSURANCE OK'D FOR ONE-FOR-10 SCRIP ISSUE.</title>
<headline>NATL INSURANCE OK'D FOR ONE-FOR-10 SCRIP ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders at the annual meeting of National Insurance, a subsidiary of National Bank, approved a one-for-ten scrip issue, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company will issue new shares capitalising asset revaluation reserves totalling 1.2 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>National Insurance will pay a dividend per share of 60 drachmas for fiscal 1996 versus 110 in the previous year.</p>
<p>Shareholders granted their approval on the absorption of affiliated Panellinios Insurance.</p>
<p>National Insurance has already absorbed NIBID Insurance, another National Bank insurance firm, while the merger with affiliated Astir Insurance is already in the works, it said.</p>
<p>National Insurance's shares will trade ex-dividend and ex-bonus on June 30. --Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
